<article class="env-proposition" id="8F1D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/8F1D">Proposition <span data-tag="8F1D">5.2.2.12</span>.</a>adjoint functor!existence of Let $f: \calC \rightarrow \calD $ be a functor between $\infty $-categories. Suppose that the induced functor of $\calH $-enriched categories $\rm {h} \it {f}: \rm {h} \it {\calC } \rightarrow \rm {h} \it {\calD }$ admits a right adjoint. Then $f$ admits a right adjoint. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      According to $(1)$ of Proposition <a href="/tag/AC42" data-tag="AC42">5.2.1.3</a>, there is a coCartesian fibration $p: \calM \rightarrow \Delta ^1$ associated to $f$. Let $\rm {h} \it {g}$ be the right adjoint of $\rm {h} \it {f}$. Applying Lemma <a href="/tag/6FFA" data-tag="6FFA">5.2.2.11</a>, we deduce that $p$ is a Cartesian fibration. Thus $p$ is an adjunction, so that $f$ has a right adjoint as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>